      "value": "*Author: Victor Crisostomo · Reviewed by: Tim Lavelle · Last updated: 2026-08-28**Jira: [SFCC-49](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-49) · Status: **Tech design***\n\n---\n\n1. Purpose & Scope\n------------------\n\nSFCC-49 asks a Site Admin to configure the full list of countries and map each country to its correct regional storefront so that address forms and the country selector have the correct country data.\n\nThis TSD describes how the country list is sourced, stored, synced to the PWA codebase, and consumed — in a way that gives admins a BM UI for management, avoids a runtime API call on first hit, and extends the existing `npm run sync:regional-config` tooling rather than introducing a new pipeline.\n\n**In scope:**\n\n* SFCC Custom Object schema for the per-storefront country list\n* Extension of `scripts/sfcc/syncRegionalConfig.mjs` to fetch and write the country list\n* New generated file `overrides/app/config/countryList.generated.ts` and its consumer\n* Override of `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` in `overrides/app/constants.ts` to wire the address form country dropdown\n* Test and Storybook gap that arises from how the `OverridesResolverPlugin` works\n\n**Out of scope (separate stories):**\n\n* The flag/storefront selector in the footer (locale selector placeholder)\n* Per-storefront Adyen checkout region selector (Global-e iframe; cannot be controlled)\n* The country selector slide-out / mismatch modal (REG-014–035)\n\n---\n\n2. Background\n-------------\n\n### 2.1 What the base template provides (and doesn't)\n\nThe base `@salesforce/retail-react-app` populates the checkout and account address form country dropdown from a constant `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` imported from `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants`:\n\nDefaultnone// node\\_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants.js\nexport const SHIPPING\\_COUNTRY\\_CODES = [\n{ value: 'CA', label: 'Canada' },\n{ value: 'US', label: 'United States' },\n]\n\nThis is the base template stub — it is **not overridden** anywhere in the Zimmermann `overrides/` directory. Every address form on every Zimmermann storefront currently shows only CA and US.\n\n`useAddressFields.jsx` (base template) imports this constant and passes it directly as the `options` array to the country `<select>` field. The constant is not fetched from SFCC Business Manager at runtime — it is a static import.\n\n### 2.2 What the existing sync script covers\n\n`npm run sync:regional-config` (`scripts/sfcc/syncRegionalConfig.mjs`) fetches live locale and currency data from SFCC via the Shopper Configurations API (SCAPI) and writes four generated files. The relevant one for this story is:\n\n* `overrides/app/config/countries.generated.ts` — per URL slug: `{ sfccSiteId, locale, currency }`\n\n`overrides/app/config/countries.ts` (Tier 1) merges this with a hand-maintained overlay that adds `shippingCountry`, `checkoutOwner`, `globalEPricing`, and `boutiqueRegion` per slug.\n\nThis config is about **which storefronts exist and how to route to them**. It is not the same as **which countries a shopper can select when filling in a delivery address on a given storefront** — that is the country list SFCC-49 is about.\n\n### 2.3 Tim Lavelle's direction (2026-08-19)\n\n> \"I think we look at managed in a SFCC Custom object, and expand the `npm run sync:regional-config` command to also add these to the PWA country mapping. None of these options will allow this to happen w/o a deployment as I don't want to introduce an API call on first hit to get the countries from Contentful or a SFCC custom object. So I think our approach is to allow them to manage it via a UI, but to reduce the API call, it needs to get synced to our codebase.\"\n\n— Tim Lavelle, [SFCC-49 comment](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-49?focusedCommentId=13913)\n\n---\n\n3. Options Considered\n---------------------\n\n| Option | Description | Verdict |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **A — PWA config only** | Hand-edited TypeScript constant in `overrides/app/config/countryList.ts`. No BM UI. | ❌ Rejected — Site Admin cannot update without a PR and code review |\n| **B — Custom Object + runtime fetch** | Store in BM, expose via custom SCAPI endpoint, fetch on every request. | ❌ Rejected — Tim explicitly declined; adds latency and a new failure mode on a critical checkout path |\n| **C — Contentful** | Store as a structured content type, fetch via CDA. | ❌ Rejected — routing config is not editorial content; Contentful integration not yet stable (SFCC-249 in progress) |\n| **✅ D — Custom Object + sync to codebase** | Store in BM (admin UI). Extend `npm run sync:regional-config` to read via OCAPI and write a generated file. No runtime API call. Deploy required after sync. | ✅ Chosen |\n\n---\n\n4. Data Model\n-------------\n\n### 4.1 SFCC Custom Object Type — `StorefrontCountryList`\n\nThe Business Manager metadata XML for importing this Custom Object type is attached to this page as **`StorefrontCountryList-metadata.xml`**.\n\n**Import path in BM:** Administration › Site Development › Import & Export › Metadata\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Object ID** (key) | String | SFCC site ID, e.g. `ZimmermannAU`. Used by the sync script as the OCAPI lookup key. |\n| `shippingCountries` | Set of String | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes, e.g. `[\"AU\",\"NZ\",\"SG\",\"JP\",...]`. Min length 2, max length 2 per entry. Mandatory. |\n| `lastSyncedAt` | String | ISO 8601 timestamp written by the sync script after each successful run. Read-only for Site Admins; useful for auditing whether the PWA is up to date. |\n\n**Scope:** Site-scoped Custom Object — one object per real SFCC site:\n\n| Object ID (key) | Storefront |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ZimmermannAU` | AU + Oceania |\n| `ZimmermannUS` | US domestic |\n| `ZimmermannUK` | UK |\n| `ZimmermannEU` | EU domestic (all four locale variants share this) |\n| `ZimmermannHK` | HK |\n| `ZimmermannME` | ME |\n\n**OCAPI read endpoint:**DefaultnoneGET /s/-/dw/data/v25\\_6/sites/{site\\_id}/custom\\_objects/StorefrontCountryList/{site\\_id}\n\n> Note: OCAPI is deprecated as of Salesforce B2C Commerce 24.7 in favour of SCAPI, but Custom Objects are not yet exposed via SCAPI — OCAPI remains the only viable server-side path for reading them.\n\n### 4.2 Sync Flow\n\nThe diagram below shows how a Site Admin edit in Business Manager flows through `npm run sync:regional-config` to the PWA address form at runtime.\n\nMacroBodyMermaidflowchart TD\nAdmin[\"🧑‍💼 Site Admin\\nCustom Object Editor\"] -->|\"edit shippingCountries\\nper SFCC site\"| CO[(\"StorefrontCountryList\\nCustom Object\\n(site-scoped)\")]\nDev[\"👩‍💻 Developer\\nnpm run sync:regional-config\"] --> Auth[\"OCAPI OAuth\\nBM client credentials → token\"]\nAuth --> Script[\"syncRegionalConfig.mjs\\nfetch → derive → atomic write\"]\nCO -->|\"GET /dw/data/v25\\_6/\\nsites/{site\\_id}/custom\\_objects/...\"| Script\nSCAPI[\"SCAPI Shopper Config\\n(existing step — locales/currencies)\"] -->|\"site config\"| Script\nScript -->|\"atomic write\\n(5 files, all-or-nothing)\"| GEN[\"📄 countryList.generated.ts ★\\n📄 countries.generated.ts\\n📄 sites.generated.js\\n📄 contentfulMapping.generated.ts\\n📄 site.generated.js\"]\nGEN -->|\"commit → PR → deploy\"| PWA[\"PWA Build\\noverrides/app/constants.ts\\noverrides SHIPPING\\_COUNTRY\\_CODES\"]\nPWA --> Form[\"✅ Address Form\\nCountry Dropdown\\ncorrect per storefront\"]\nstyle CO fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#3b82f6\nstyle GEN fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#10b981\nstyle Form fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a\nstyle Script fill:#f9fafb,stroke:#6b7280,stroke-width:2px\n> ⚠️ **A deploy is always required after running the sync** — the country list is baked into the bundle, not fetched at runtime. This is intentional (Tim Lavelle, 2026-08-19).\n\n### 4.3 Generated File Shape — `overrides/app/config/countryList.generated.ts`\n\nKeyed by **real SFCC site ID** (multiple PWA URL slugs may share one site — e.g. all four EU locale slugs map to `ZimmermannEU`):\n\nDefaultnone// AUTO-GENERATED by `npm run sync:regional-config` — do not edit by hand.\nexport const GENERATED\\_COUNTRY\\_LIST = {\nZimmermannAU: ['AU', 'NZ', 'SG', 'JP', ...],\nZimmermannUS: ['US'],\nZimmermannUK: ['GB'],\nZimmermannEU: ['DE', 'FR', 'IT', 'ES', 'NL', ...],\nZimmermannHK: ['HK'],\nZimmermannME: ['AE', 'SA', 'QA', 'KW', ...],\n} as const;\n\n### 4.4 Consumer File — `overrides/app/config/countryList.ts`\n\nDefaultnoneimport { GENERATED\\_COUNTRY\\_LIST } from './countryList.generated';\nimport { COUNTRIES } from './countries';\n/\\*\\*\n\\* Per-URL-slug list of ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 shipping country codes.\n\\* Used to populate address form country dropdowns and (future) the storefront\n\\* country selector.\n\\*/\nexport const COUNTRY\\_LIST: Record<string, readonly string[]> = Object.fromEntries(\nObject.entries(COUNTRIES).map(([slug, config]) => [\nslug,\nGENERATED\\_COUNTRY\\_LIST[config.sfccSiteId as keyof typeof GENERATED\\_COUNTRY\\_LIST] ?? [],\n]),\n);\n\n---\n\n5. PWA Integration\n------------------\n\n### 5.1 Address Form Country Dropdown\n\n`useAddressFields.jsx` (base template) populates the country `<select>` from `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` imported from `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants`.\n\nThe `OverridesResolverPlugin` (webpack plugin backing `ccExtensibility`) intercepts imports of `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants` when the **issuer is outside the `overrides/` directory** — which covers `useAddressFields.jsx` in `node_modules`. Creating `overrides/app/constants.ts` is therefore sufficient to override `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` in the production build and dev server without modifying the base template file.\n\nDefaultnone// overrides/app/constants.ts\nexport \\* from '@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants';\nimport { useCountryConfig } from './hooks/useCountryConfig';\nimport { COUNTRY\\_LIST } from './config/countryList';\n/\\*\\*\n\\* Site-aware shipping country options for the address form country dropdown.\n\\* Overrides the base template stub (CA + US only).\n\\*/\nexport function useShippingCountryCodes(): Array<{ value: string; label: string }> {\nconst { urlSlug, locale } = useCountryConfig();\nconst codes = COUNTRY\\_LIST[urlSlug] ?? [];\nreturn codes.map((code) => ({\nvalue: code,\nlabel: new Intl.DisplayNames([locale, 'en'], { type: 'region' }).of(code) ?? code,\n}));\n}\n> Note: `Intl.DisplayNames` uses the site locale first (e.g. `fr-FR`, `de-DE`) with `'en'` as fallback, so country names render in the storefront's language automatically.\n\n### 5.2 Partial Override of `useAddressFields`\n\nBecause `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` in the base is a static import (not a hook), replacing it with a site-aware hook requires a minimal override of `useAddressFields.jsx` at `overrides/app/components/forms/useAddressFields.ts`.\n\nThe override copies the base file, converts to TypeScript, and replaces only the `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` import line and its usage in the `countryCode` field definition with a call to `useShippingCountryCodes()`. No other logic changes.\n\n**Copy-first rule applies** — per AGENTS.md, the base file must be copied, converted to TypeScript, and confirmed rendering before functional changes are made.\n\n### 5.3 Storybook / Vitest Gap\n\nThe `OverridesResolverPlugin` does **not** run in Storybook or Vitest:\n\n* Storybook's `main.js` aliases `@salesforce/retail-react-app` straight to `node_modules`\n* Vitest has no resolver\n\n`overrides/app/constants.ts` is therefore bypassed in both environments. Any story or Vitest test rendering a component that uses `useAddressFields` will see the base stub (CA + US), not the Zimmermann country list.\n\n**Mitigation:** mock `@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants` at the test/story level:\n\nDefaultnonevi.mock('@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants', async (importOriginal) => {\nconst actual = await importOriginal<typeof import('@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants')>();\nreturn { ...actual, SHIPPING\\_COUNTRY\\_CODES: [{ value: 'AU', label: 'Australia' }] };\n});\n\nThis is the same pattern already used for `ZimmIcon` (documented in `.claude/rules/testing.md`).\n\n---\n\n6. Out of Scope — Flag / Storefront Selector\n--------------------------------------------\n\nTim asked whether the country list is reachable to populate the **flag selector** in the navigation bar. The locale/flag selector in `BottomBar` is currently a hardcoded placeholder (`'Australia (AUD) / ENG'`) — the locale selector is a **future story**.\n\nWhen it is built:\n\n* Use `COUNTRIES` from `overrides/app/config/countries.ts` for the list of available **storefronts** (routing destinations)\n* Use `COUNTRY_LIST` from `overrides/app/config/countryList.ts` for the full list of shippable-to countries per storefront\n\n**The Adyen checkout region selector cannot be controlled** — Global-e checkout is an iframe and the region selector inside it is owned entirely by Global-e.\n\n---\n\n7. Sync Script Extension\n------------------------\n\n### 7.1 New OCAPI Auth Helper in `_shared.mjs`\n\nThe existing sync uses SCAPI + SLAS tokens. SFCC Custom Objects are read via **OCAPI Data API**, which uses a different client-credentials flow (`POST /dw/oauth2/access_token` with a BM API client ID + secret).\n\nA new `getOcapiToken(siteId)` helper is added to `scripts/sfcc/_shared.mjs`, using the existing BM API client credentials — two new env vars that reference the already-configured client:\n\nDefaultnoneCOMMERCE\\_API\\_BM\\_CLIENT\\_ID # scope:shared\nCOMMERCE\\_API\\_BM\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET # scope:shared\n\nBoth are added to `.env.sample` with empty values. The existing BM API client needs its OCAPI Data API settings updated to include read access for Custom Objects (see implementation step 2).\n\n### 7.2 New Fetch Function\n\nDefaultnoneasync function fetchCountryListGenerated(overlay) {\nconst realSiteIds = [...new Set(overlay.map((s) => s.sfccSiteId ?? s.id))];\nconst generated = {};\nfor (const siteId of realSiteIds) {\nconst token = await getOcapiToken(siteId);\nconst url = `${SFCC\\_BASE\\_URL}/s/-/dw/data/v25\\_6/sites/${siteId}/custom\\_objects/StorefrontCountryList/${siteId}`;\nconst res = await fetch(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } });\nif (res.status === 404) throw new Error(`StorefrontCountryList object not found for '${siteId}' — import the metadata XML and populate the object in BM first.`);\nif (!res.ok) throw new Error(`OCAPI fetch failed for ${siteId}: ${res.status}`);\nconst obj = await res.json();\nconst codes = obj.c\\_shippingCountries ?? [];\nif (!codes.length) throw new Error(`StorefrontCountryList for '${siteId}' is empty — populate in BM first.`);\ngenerated[siteId] = codes;\n}\nreturn generated;\n}\n> Error handling distinguishes `404 ObjectTypeNotFoundException` (metadata XML not imported) from `404 CustomObjectNotFoundException` (object key missing), per the OCAPI v25\\_6 fault spec.\n\n### 7.3 New TARGETS Entry\n\nDefaultnoneTARGETS.countryList = {\nfile: resolve(REPO\\_ROOT, 'overrides/app/config/countryList.generated.ts'),\nformat: 'ts',\nexportName: 'GENERATED\\_COUNTRY\\_LIST',\nconsumer: 'overrides/app/config/countryList.ts',\n};\n\nAdded to the `outputs` array in `main()` alongside the existing four targets. All-or-nothing write pattern is preserved.\n\n---\n\n8. File Inventory\n-----------------\n\n| File | Action | Tier | Approval |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `scripts/sfcc/syncRegionalConfig.mjs` | Extend — OCAPI fetch + new TARGETS entry | **Tier 1** | Integration lead |\n| `scripts/sfcc/_shared.mjs` | Extend — `getOcapiToken()` helper | **Tier 1** | Integration lead |\n| `overrides/app/config/countryList.generated.ts` | New — auto-generated | n/a | — |\n| `overrides/app/config/countryList.ts` | New — consumer | Tier 4 | — |\n| `overrides/app/constants.ts` | New — overrides `SHIPPING_COUNTRY_CODES` | Tier 4 | — |\n| `overrides/app/components/forms/useAddressFields.ts` | New — minimal override (copy-first) | Tier 4 | — |\n| `.env.sample` | Extend — add two new BM env vars | **Tier 1** | Integration lead |\n\n---\n\n9. Implementation Steps\n-----------------------\n\n1. **BM setup***(SI Partner / Integration lead)* — Import `StorefrontCountryList-metadata.xml` (attached below) into BM. Populate one object per real SFCC site with the agreed country list from the [Confluence country table](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/255852545/CountryListper+Storefront).\n2. **OCAPI Data API settings***(Victor Crisostomo)* — In BM, Administration › Site Development › Open Commerce API Settings › Data API, add read permission for `/sites/*/custom_objects/**` to the existing BM API client.\n3. **Env vars** — Add `COMMERCE_API_BM_CLIENT_ID` and `COMMERCE_API_BM_CLIENT_SECRET` to `.env.sample`; run `npm run env -- init` locally.\n4. **`_shared.mjs`** — Add `getOcapiToken()` helper *(Integration lead approval)*.\n5. **`syncRegionalConfig.mjs`** — Add `fetchCountryListGenerated`, new TARGETS entry, extended `checkEnv` *(Integration lead approval)*.\n6. **Run sync** — `npm run sync:regional-config` to generate `countryList.generated.ts`.\n7. **`countryList.ts`** — Create consumer file (§4.4).\n8. **`overrides/app/constants.ts`** — Create constants override with `useShippingCountryCodes` hook (§5.1).\n9. **`useAddressFields.ts`** — Minimal copy-first override; confirm rendering before functional changes (§5.2).\n10. **Tests** — Add `vi.mock` for any Vitest test / Storybook story rendering the address form country dropdown (§5.3).\n11. **PR** — Target `feature/SFCC-49-country-list`. Run `cr review --light --base develop` before commit.\n\n---\n\n10. Open Items\n--------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Blocking? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm final agreed country list per storefront in the [Confluence country table](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/255852545/CountryListper+Storefront) | Jasmijn / Emma | ✅ Yes — BM setup (step 1) cannot start without it |\n| 2 | ~~Confirm SFCC BM API client ID + secret and OCAPI permission set~~ — **Resolved.** Existing BM API client will be reused. OCAPI Data API settings to be updated by Victor to add Custom Objects read permission. | — | ✅ Closed |\n| 3 | ~~Confirm SFCC OCAPI Data API version~~ — **Resolved.** Confirmed v25\\_6. Endpoint corrected to `/s/-/dw/data/v25_6/sites/{site_id}/custom_objects/StorefrontCountryList/{site_id}`. | — | ✅ Closed |\n| 4 | ~~Country label language~~ — **Resolved.** `Intl.DisplayNames` uses site locale first with `'en'` fallback (§5.1). | — | ✅ Closed |\n| 5 | Raise a separate Jira for the flag/storefront selector story if not already captured | Jasmijn | No |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
