    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nMulti-site and locale configuration in BM controls how Zimmermann's seven storefronts are isolated and configured. Timezone configuration is critical for sale-day launch scheduling — wrong timezone means a sale fires at the wrong time across boutique operations and timed communications. This was explicitly flagged as a pain point in the merchandising deep dive.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Multi-Site Configuration in Business Manager](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/GlobalizationandLocalization/Multisite.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Locales and Regional Settings](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/GlobalizationandLocalization/Locales.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Trailhead:** [Get Started with Commerce Cloud Business Manager — Administration](https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/cc-digital-for-developers/cc-business-manager)\n\n**⚠️ Risk note:** Timezone misconfiguration on any site causes sale launches, promotion activations, and price book activations to fire at the wrong local time. Zimmermann's launch-day operations are tightly coordinated across time zones — this must be exact.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### Sites Created & Configured (BM: Administration → Sites → Manage Sites)\n\n1\nc20e6c8119ca\ncomplete\nAU site created and configured\n\n2\n5b0705090b61\ncomplete\nUK site created and configured\n\n3\n85718b12bf5c\ncomplete\nUS Domestic site created and configured\n\n4\n890987bd34eb\ncomplete\nUS Intl (Global-e) site created and configured\n\n552063992301\n552063992301\ncomplete\nEU Domestic site created and configured\n\n5\nb027924b5e2c\ncomplete\nEU Intl (Global-e) site created and configured\n\n6\nbf35c694097b\ncomplete\nME site created and configured\n\n### Per-Site Settings (verify for each site)\n\n7\n888977b35df8\ncomplete\nDefault locale set correctly per site\n\n8\n7d41c1704831\ncomplete\nSupported locales assigned per site\n\n9\n848235bdc06b\ncomplete\nCurrency configured correctly per site (AUD, GBP, USD, EUR)\n\n10\nfee587096b0d\ncomplete\nAU timezone set to `Australia/Sydney`\n\n11\nd89896c511df\ncomplete\nUK timezone set to `Europe/London`\n\n12\nb9b76f49b7dd\ncomplete\nUS timezone set to `America/New_York` (or as agreed with ops team)\n\n13\n8becd01b564a\ncomplete\nEU timezone set to `Europe/Paris` (or as agreed with ops team)\n\n14\n5a90fe5b732c\ncomplete\nME timezone set to `Asia/Dubai`\n\n### Locale Routing\n\n15\n07e0978741bb\nincomplete\nLocale path prefixes correct per site (e.g. `/en-AU/`, `/en-GB/`, `/fr-FR/`)\n\n16\n9a2ca684d907\nincomplete\nCountry-to-site routing logic configured\n\n17\n7197c93b6903\nincomplete\nLanguage switcher on storefront routes to correct locale URLs\n\n### TransPerfect / GlobalLink Translation\n\n18\n09f1d9c302b9\nincomplete\nGlobalLink WebStore connector configured in BM for SFCC locale fields\n\n19\n6fad2581ea68\nincomplete\nMuleSoft confirmed to write only to the EN master locale field in SFCC (translated values treated as SFCC-owned — Option A alignment)\n\n20\n69c660befaee\nincomplete\nTranslated locale fields not being overwritten by AP21 sync job\n\n### Organisation-Level Settings (BM: Administration → Global Preferences)\n\n21\n771e77d74473\ncomplete\nGlobal locales and regional settings configured\n\n22\n040d325b3d01\nincomplete\nOrganisation-level preferences reviewed and not relying on defaults\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |",
